      "sequence": 2315,
      "title": "(review)",
      "headword": "(review)",
      "romanization": "(review)",
      "gloss": "three joints and two constants — everything reporting asks of you, said aloud rather than laid out in a table",
      "script": "latin",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:e17f0f7b146772d0",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two forms first, because the rest is built on them. He said. (Dijo.) They said. (Dijeron — no i.)"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three chants. Say each one, then say what it is for."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "First. Dijo que trabajaba. — a statement goes in on que, and que may never be dropped."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Second. Preguntó si trabajaba. — a yes-or-no question goes in on si, the same si that opens a condition."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Third. Preguntó dónde trabajaba. — a question that starts with an asking word brings its own joint, accent and all."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "grammar",
          "title": "Grammar Lens: the two things that never change",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Whatever the joint, two things are true of all three chants."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One. The inner verb steps back into the imperfect — because a report says what was going on when somebody spoke."
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two. The question marks go. A report tells; it does not ask. And yet the accent on dónde stays, because that accent was never marking the sentence — it marks the word that does the asking."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the three chants, in order, without looking",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the three chants, in order, without looking]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "repeat",
              "times": 2,
              "source": "[REPEAT x2]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C57-repaso-reportar-que",
              "prompt": "Which joint reports a statement?",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-REPORTED-QUE-OBLIGATORY"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 10,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "que",
                "que, and it cannot be dropped"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "And English may drop that; Spanish may not.",
                "incorrect": "Que."
              }
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C57-repaso-reportar-si",
              "prompt": "Which joint reports a yes-or-no question?",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-REPORTED-YESNO-SI"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 10,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "si",
                "si, the same one as in conditions"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "One word holding something open.",
                "incorrect": "Si."
              }
            },
            {
              "kind": "activity",
              "scored": true,
              "id": "ES-C57-repaso-reportar-wh",
              "prompt": "And when the question already starts with donde?",
              "assesses": [
                "ES-GRAMMAR-REPORTED-WH-ACCENT"
              ],
              "responseSeconds": 13,
              "acceptedResponses": [
                "donde is the joint",
                "no que and no si, donde does it"
              ],
              "feedback": {
                "correct": "It was already at the front; it stays.",
                "incorrect": "Donde is the joint -- no que, no si."
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Which tense does the inner verb land in, every time? (The imperfect.)"
            },
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "And one word to keep, for the pleasure of it: what is the j of dijo, historically? (A Latin x. Dīxit, dixo, dijo.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
